    "summary": "Ferocious Other One night with stellar Dark Star and Cosmic Charlie",
    "blurb": "The show erupts from the opening Cryptical Envelopment into a relentless flow of improvisation, highlighted by a ferocious The Other One and a soaring Dark Star. Cosmic Charlie rages through Set 1 while Dupree's Diamond Blues and St. Stephen shine in Set 2, ending with a flawless Hey Jude encore.",
    "review": "On March 1, 1969 at the Fillmore West the Dead delivered one of their most intense early‑period performances. From the opening Cryptical Envelopment/Other One sandwich to the unbroken energy that carries through New Potato Caboose and Cosmic Charlie, the band barely pauses, creating a fever‑pitch marathon that feels almost continuous. The second set offers a classic 1969 blend: an acoustic‑driven Dupree's Diamond Blues segues into Mountains of the Moon before exploding into a radiant Dark Star that rolls straight into Saint Stephen and a powerful, if brief, rendition of The Eleven. Phil Lesh’s bass roars on fire, matching Jerry’s ferocious SG tone, while Brent’s organ adds texture throughout, even shining on the heartfelt Hey Jude encore. Across all six soundboard sources the multitrack capture (gd69-03-01.sbd.16track.kaplan) stands out for its pristine clarity and full‑band balance, making this a must‑listen run for any Deadhead seeking high‑energy improvisation at its peak.",
